Z||000015||Raydar||05-06-2000||06:21 PM||||Several (many?) times a day. <BR>A great deal of my day consists of installing NT and apps on PCs, in my office. Much of the installation is automated. I can start the script and let it fly. All I have to do for the next hour or two is make sure the script doesn't blow up for some reason. <BR>While it's running, I'll frequently scan the Forum on my "own" PC. If they ever start logging everyone's internet usage, I suspect I'll raise some eyebrows.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>I don't believe that's the case, though. There are several thousand of us in the building. I suspect that all they scrutinize are selected "adult" sites. Most are filtered, anyway.<P>Hi. My name's Raydar, and I'm a Fieroholic.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 05-06-2000).]||||reg||6
